# Normalise line endings to LF everywhere, in the repository *and* in the
# working tree, on every platform. Without this, Git on Windows defaults to
# core.autocrlf=true and checks files out with CRLF, which breaks byte-exact
# test fixtures and shell scripts ("bad interpreter: /bin/sh^M").
# Modern Windows editors all handle LF, so forcing it costs nothing.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
# batch files are the exception: cmd.exe misreads labels and long lines in
# LF-only .cmd/.bat files, so they check out with CRLF
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Binary assets
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.gif binary
*.msi binary
*.exe binary
*.londopy binary
*.londo binary
